Gretchen, Warrick,<br />
<br />
The opposition to the Fenwick Alder fee application goes in Friday and runs=
 on two independent grounds, either of which disposes of it.<br />
<br />
Eligibility. Respondent is not an eligible party. Its net worth as shown in=
 its own audited balance sheet was $9.4 million at the date the proceeding =
was instituted, above the $7,000,000 ceiling. Respondent's declaration comp=
utes net worth after deducting the amount it expected to spend on the defen=
se, which is not how the calculation works and which no adjudicator has eve=
r accepted.<br />
<br />
Substantial justification. The Division's position was reasonable in law an=
d in fact when taken and remained so. The proceeding was dismissed because =
the adjudicator credited the testimony of Respondent's former operations ma=
nager over documentary inferences the Division drew from Respondent's own r=
ecords. Losing a credibility contest is not the same as having had no reaso=
nable basis to bring the claim, and the standard is satisfied where a reaso=
nable person could think the position correct.<br />
<br />
I am not asking for a hearing on the application and I do not think one is =
needed.<br />
<br />
Anneke Vogelsang<br />
Assistant Director, Division of Enforcement, New York Regional Office